const pct=v=>(100*v).toFixed(1)+'%',brier=v=>v.toFixed(4),interval=v=>v.map(x=>x.toFixed(2)).join(' to ');
export function renderDirectionEvidence(m){
 const root=document.getElementById('direction-evidence');
 root.innerHTML=`<article class="panel direction-evidence"><div class="panel-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">DIRECTION V2 · SIX MONTHS OF DFLD</div><h2>Better short-range forecasts.<br>Measured against reported operations.</h2></div><span class="pill">HELD-OUT TEST</span></div><p>DFLD-reported directions replace weather-rule labels for this classifier. The original model and challenge rules are re-scored on exactly the same later hours. Models were selected on validation Brier before these test results were inspected.</p><div class="dfld-kpis"><div class="dfld-kpi"><span>HISTORY</span><strong>${m.days} days</strong><p>30 April–29 October 2026</p></div><div class="dfld-kpi"><span>DIRECTION REPORTS</span><strong>${m.knownHalfHourBins.toLocaleString()}</strong><p>Half-hour observations</p></div><div class="dfld-kpi"><span>1H ACCURACY GAIN</span><strong>+${m.horizons[0].accuracyGainVsLegacyPp.toFixed(2)} pp</strong><p>Against the frozen original model</p></div><div class="dfld-kpi"><span>6H ACCURACY GAIN</span><strong>+${m.horizons[1].accuracyGainVsLegacyPp.toFixed(2)} pp</strong><p>On the same reported-direction hours</p></div></div>
 <div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Lead</th><th>Test hours</th><th>New accuracy</th><th>Original / rules</th><th>New Brier ↓</th><th>Original / rules Brier ↓</th></tr></thead><tbody>${m.horizons.map(h=>{const t=h.targets;return `<tr><td>${h.horizonHours}h</td><td>${h.testRows}</td><td><strong>${pct(t.dfldModel.accuracy)}</strong></td><td>${pct(t.legacyModel.accuracy)} / ${pct(t.weatherRules.accuracy)}</td><td class="${h.brierImprovementVsLegacy<0?'regression':''}">${brier(t.dfldModel.brier)}</td><td>${brier(t.legacyModel.brier)} / ${brier(t.weatherRules.brier)}</td></tr>`;}).join('')}</tbody></table></div>
 <p><strong>The gain has limits.</strong> The new model beats the weather-rule baseline at all four tested leads. Compared with the original model, 24h accuracy is unchanged and probability error is worse at 24h and 48h. Scores are not calibrated operational certainty. These actual-direction scores cannot be compared directly with the older weather-proxy benchmark below.</p>
 <details><summary>Evaluation design, coverage &amp; uncertainty</summary><p>UTC target dates: train 30 April–31 August; validate 4–26 September; test 30 September–29 October 2026. Splits have 72-hour gaps. Train-only normalization; validation-only feature and regularization selection. The target is the reported half-hour bin beginning at the valid forecast hour, not an exact switch time.</p><p>Europe/Berlin was empirically checked against 240 METAR bins across summer and winter. The ambiguous 25 October clock-change date is excluded. DFLD labels are never forecast inputs. Missing or variable METAR direction, unavailable trends and forecast gaps are excluded; coverage below describes the remaining eligible hours.</p><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Lead</th><th>Train / validation</th><th>Test coverage</th><th>Accuracy gain 95% interval (pp)</th><th>Brier improvement 95% interval</th></tr></thead><tbody>${m.horizons.map(h=>`<tr><td>${h.horizonHours}h</td><td>${h.trainRows} / ${h.validationRows}</td><td>${pct(h.testCoverage)}</td><td>${interval(h.uncertaintyVsLegacy.accuracyGainPercentagePoints95)}</td><td>${h.uncertaintyVsLegacy.brierImprovement95.map(brier).join(' to ')}</td></tr>`).join('')}</tbody></table></div><p>Intervals use 1,000 paired daily-block bootstrap draws against the original model; positive values favor v2. They account for within-day correlation, not all seasonal or multi-day dependence. Six months have limited seasonal coverage. Archived ICON offsets predate forecast origin by at least 18h; exact delivery timestamps are unavailable. Live weather is fresher than backtest weather, so this retrospective evaluation does not prove live performance.</p><p><strong>RWY 18 remains unchanged:</strong> no confirmed closure labels were obtained. Zero departures never become closure targets. The next change hour is still an unvalidated crossing of direction scores.</p></details>
 <div class="audit-links"><a href="data/direction-metrics.json" download>Full scores &amp; experiment plan ↓</a><a href="data/direction-test-predictions.json" download>Held-out predictions ↓</a><a href="data/direction-model.json" download>Direction model ↓</a><a href="data/dfld-time-audit.json" download>Clock audit ↓</a></div></article>`;
}
